    <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:2rem;">
      <a href="/contact/" class="cta-button">Get Free Quote</a>
      <a href={`${WHATSAPP_URL}?text=Hi%20SDF%20Clothing%2C%20I%20need%20a%20quote%20for%20dye-house-service`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="whatsapp-cta">
        <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
          <path d="M17.472 14.382c-.297-.149-1.758-.867-2.03-.967-.273-.099-.471-.148-.67.15-.197.297-.767.966-.94 1.164-.173.199-.347.223-.644.075-.297-.15-1.255-.463-2.39-1.475-.883-.788-1.48-1.761-1.653-2.059-.173-.297-.018-.458.13-.606.134-.133.298-.347.446-.52.149-.174.198-.298.298-.497.099-.198.05-.371-.025-.52-.075-.149-.669-1.612-.916-2.207-.242-.579-.487-.5-.669-.51-.173-.008-.371-.01-.57-.01-.198 0-.52.074-.792.372-.272.297-1.04 1.016-1.04 2.479 0 1.462 1.065 2.875 1.213 3.074.149.198 2.096 3.2 5.077 4.487.709.306 1.262.489 1.694.625.712.227 1.36.195 1.871.118.571-.085 1.758-.719 2.006-1.413.248-.694.248-1.289.173-1.413-.074-.124-.272-.198-.57-.347m-5.421 7.403h-.004a9.87 9.87 0 01-5.031-1.378l-.361-.214-3.741.982.998-3.648-.235-.374a9.86 9.86 0 01-1.51-5.26c.001-5.45 4.436-9.884 9.888-9.884 2.64 0 5.122 1.03 6.988 2.898a9.825 9.825 0 012.893 6.994c-.003 5.45-4.437 9.884-9.885 9.884m8.413-18.297A11.815 11.815 0 0012.05 0C5.495 0 .16 5.335.157 11.892c0 2.096.547 4.142 1.588 5.945L.057 24l6.305-1.654a11.882 11.882 0 005.683 1.448h.005c6.554 0 11.89-5.335 11.893-11.893a11.821 11.821 0 00-3.48-8.413z"/>
        </svg>
        WhatsApp Now
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Quick Stats Section -->
<section style="padding:4rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:1px;background:#000000;">
      <div style="background:#000;padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
        <div style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:200;color:#e00;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">80K</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FFFFFF;">KG Daily Capacity</div>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#000;padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
        <div style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:200;color:#e00;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">GOTS</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FFFFFF;">Organic Certified</div>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#000;padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
        <div style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:200;color:#e00;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">4+</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FFFFFF;">Dye Types</div>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#000;padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
        <div style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:200;color:#e00;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">B2B</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FFFFFF;">Contract Dyeing</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- What is Dye House Service Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Service Overview</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">What is a Dye House Service?</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      A dye house is a specialized facility dedicated to dyeing textiles at commercial scale. Unlike garment manufacturers that offer dyeing as part of full production, a dye house focuses exclusively on the dyeing process | serving fabric mills, wholesalers, and garment manufacturers who need professional dyeing as a standalone service.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Our dye house in Bangladesh operates 24/7 with computerized color matching, automated chemical dosing, and energy-efficient machinery. We process fabric, yarn, and finished garments through reactive, disperse, vat, sulphur, and pigment dyeing processes | all certified to GOTS and OEKO-TEX standards.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Difference from Dyeing Service Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Service Comparison</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">How Dye House Service Differs from Dyeing Service</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Dye house service is B2B-focused on commercial scale operations. Fabric mills send greige fabric for bulk dyeing before knitting or weaving. Wholesalers contract dye houses for large color batches. Garment manufacturers use dye houses for fabric preparation before cut-and-sew.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Dyeing service (our other page) is broader | serving fashion brands who need garment dyeing, sample dyeing, or color development as part of their production. Dye house is for industrial dyeing contracts. Minimums are higher, capacity is larger, and operations are designed for throughput rather than customization.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Capacity and Scale Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Production Capacity</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Capacity and Scale</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Our dye house operates at commercial scale with multiple production lines:
    </p>
    <ul style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.9;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:1.5rem 0;max-width:800px;">
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative;">
        <span style="color:#e00;position:absolute;left:0;">✓</span>
        Fabric dyeing capacity: 50,000-80,000 kg per day
      </li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative;">
        <span style="color:#e00;position:absolute;left:0;">✓</span>
        Yarn dyeing capacity: 15,000-25,000 kg per day
      </li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative;">
        <span style="color:#e00;position:absolute;left:0;">✓</span>
        Garment dyeing capacity: 10,000-20,000 pieces per day
      </li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:0.75rem;padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative;">
        <span style="color:#e00;position:absolute;left:0;">✓</span>
        Lab dip development: 200-300 lab dips per week
      </li>
      <li style="padding-left:1.5rem;position:relative;">
        <span style="color:#e00;position:absolute;left:0;">✓</span>
        Multiple dye houses for different fiber types to avoid contamination
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Contract Dyeing Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">B2B Services</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Contract Dyeing for Fabric Mills</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Fabric mills use our contract dyeing service when they need additional capacity or specialized dyeing capabilities. You send greige fabric, we dye it to your specification, and return it ready for your finishing processes.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Long-term contracts available with guaranteed capacity allocation, priority scheduling, and fixed pricing. We maintain color records for repeat orders to ensure consistency across seasons.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Bulk Dyeing Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Wholesale Services</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Bulk Dyeing for Wholesalers</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Wholesalers and trading companies use our bulk dyeing service to create stock fabric in popular colors. We dye large batches that can be split across multiple buyers or held as inventory for just-in-time delivery.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Bulk dyeing offers cost advantages through economies of scale. Minimums are higher but per-kg pricing is lower. We can consolidate orders from multiple buyers using the same color to help smaller buyers access bulk pricing.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Dye Types Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Dyeing Capabilities</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Dye Types We Offer</h2>
    </div>
    
    <h3 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:400;color:#e00;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Reactive Dyeing</h3>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.92rem;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      For cotton, linen, rayon, and other natural fibers. Reactive dyes form chemical bonds with fiber molecules for excellent wash fastness and color vibrancy. Standard for most cotton dyeing applications.
    </p>

    <h3 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:400;color:#e00;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Disperse Dyeing</h3>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.92rem;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      For polyester, acetate, and other synthetic fibers. Disperse dyes are non-ionic and penetrate synthetic fibers at high temperature. Essential for polyester and polyester-blend fabrics.
    </p>

    <h3 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:400;color:#e00;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Vat Dyeing</h3>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.92rem;margin-bottom:2rem;">
      For maximum colorfastness on cotton and rayon. Vat dyes are insoluble in water and require reduction-oxidation process. Provides excellent resistance to light, washing, and chlorine. Premium option for workwear and uniforms.
    </p>

    <h3 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:400;color:#e00;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Sulphur Dyeing</h3>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.92rem;">
      For cotton and rayon in deep colors like black, navy, and brown. Sulphur dyes are economical for dark shades with good wash fastness. Commonly used for denim and workwear fabrics.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Common Questions</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    </div>
    
    <div style="max-width:800px;">
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What is the difference between dye house service and dyeing service?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Dye house service focuses on commercial scale B2B operations for fabric mills, wholesalers, and garment manufacturers who need dyeing as a standalone service. Dyeing service is broader and can include garment dyeing for fashion brands. Dye house is for bulk industrial dyeing contracts.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What is your daily dyeing capacity?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Our dye house can process 50,000-80,000 kg of fabric per day across multiple dye houses. Yarn dyeing capacity is 15,000-25,000 kg daily. We handle both large-scale contract dyeing for fabric mills and smaller bulk orders for wholesalers.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Do you offer contract dyeing for fabric mills?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Yes. We provide contract dyeing services for fabric mills who need additional capacity or specialized dyeing. You can send greige fabric and we return dyed fabric to your specification. Long-term contracts available with guaranteed capacity allocation.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What dye types do you offer?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">We offer reactive dyeing for cotton and natural fibers, disperse dyeing for polyester and synthetics, vat dyeing for maximum colorfastness, sulphur dyeing for cotton and rayon, and pigment dyeing for vintage effects. Each dye type is selected based on fiber content and end-use requirements.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What is your minimum order for dye house service?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">For fabric dyeing: 500 kg minimum per color for contract dyeing, 200 kg for bulk orders. For yarn dyeing: 300 kg minimum per color. For garment dyeing: 500 pieces minimum. We can sometimes consolidate smaller orders across buyers using similar colors.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Can you handle specialized dyeing requirements?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Yes. Our dye house handles specialized requirements including double dyeing for depth, cross-dyeing for blended fabrics, garment dyeing for finished pieces, and specialty wash effects. We have dedicated production lines for different dye types to avoid contamination.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Need commercial-scale dye house service for your fabric mill or wholesale business? <a href="/contact/" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:underline;">Contact SDF Clothing here</a> with your dyeing requirements | fabric type, quantity, dye type preference, and certification needs. We will send capacity availability, pricing, and contract terms within 48 hours. Free consultation.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Internal Link Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;">
  <div class="container">
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      For garment-focused dyeing services, read our <a href="/dyeing-service" style="color:#e00;text-decoration:underline;">garment dyeing service guide</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>


    
    <section style="padding:2rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);margin-top:2rem"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 1.5rem"><h2 style="font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);margin-bottom:1rem">Related Services</h2><nav aria-label="Related pages"><ul style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.75rem;list-style:none;padding:0"><li><a href="/low-moq-clothing-manufacturers/" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Low MOQ Manufacturers</a></li><li><a href="/private-label-clothing-manufacturer" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Private Label</a></li><li><a href="/clothing-manufacturers-for-startups/" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Startup Manufacturers</a></li><li><a href="/oem-clothing-manufacturer" style="color:var(--color-primary)">OEM Manufacturing</a></li><li><a href="/sustainable-clothing-manufacturers/" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Sustainable Manufacturing</a></li><li><a href="/certifications" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Certifications</a></li><li><a href="/quality-inspection-service" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Quality Inspection</a></li><li><a href="/tech-pack-service" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Tech Pack Service</a></li><li><a href="/sampling-service" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Sampling Service</a></li><li><a href="/full-package-production/" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Full Package Production</a></li><li><a href="/tools/price-calculator/" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Price Calculator</a></li><li><a href="/contact/" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Get a Quote</a></li></ul></nav></div></section>
<section style="padding:3rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border)"><div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 1.5rem"><h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);font-weight:600;color:var(--color-text);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Why Partner with SDF Clothing?</h2><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">Our dye house operates inside the same facility as cutting and sewing, not as a separate subcontracted unit several transport legs away. That proximity shortens the time between lab dip approval and bulk dyeing, and keeps color-batch consistency under one quality control system. GOTS, OEKO-TEX Standard 100, BSCI, WRAP, and ISO 9001 certification apply.</p><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">We run both reactive dyeing, suited to cotton and other cellulosic fibers, and disperse dyeing for polyester and other synthetics, choosing the process based on your fabric composition rather than limiting you to whatever a single subcontracted dye house offers. Minimum order is 300 pieces per style, covering lab dip development through bulk dyeing and export documentation.</p><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem">Dyeing-heavy programs benefit disproportionately from Bangladesh's trade position, since color and finishing steps add cost that tariffs then apply against. A 20% US tariff cap from late 2025 and continued EU duty-free access under Everything But Arms through November 2029 — despite LDC graduation that same month in 2026 — both help offset that added processing cost.</p><p style="color:var(--color-text-muted);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2rem">Ready to start? <a href="/contact/" style="color:var(--color-primary)">Request a sample</a> or <a href="/contact/" style="color:var(--color-primary)">contact our team</a> for a detailed FOB quote within 48 hours.</p></div></section>
